// whistle.granule
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// THE SELF-HOSTING PATTERN for granule authors (docs/01 chapter 22): a
// third-party granule has no language pack to lean on, so it carries its
// own grammar AND its own wording per language, each in a `when language`
// group. The group matching the game's language joins the build; the
// others vanish at combine time and cost nothing. A game summons this
// file by name from its own directory:
//
//     summon "whistle.granule"
//
// and the player can WHISTLE (English), PFEIFE (German), or SILBA
// (Spanish), each answered natively. A story reskins any line by
// redefining its msg_ block, most-specific-wins as always. The logic, if
// a granule has any, stays OUTSIDE the groups, written once; only words
// belong inside.

when language "english"
    verb "whistle"
        whistling

    block msg_whistling()
        say "You whistle a few bright notes into the quiet."

when language "german"
    verb "pfeife", "pfeif"
        whistling

    block msg_whistling()
        say "Du pfeifst ein paar helle Töne in die Stille."

when language "spanish"
    verb "silba", "silbar"
        whistling

    block msg_whistling()
        say "Silbas unas notas claras en el silencio."

// The behavior, once, language-free: the groups above only bring words.
on whistling
    msg_whistling
    stop
